1
00:00:27,291 --> 00:00:28,291
Oh, no!

2
00:00:29,791 --> 00:00:31,083
What happened?

3
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:35,416
Mom!

4
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,083
No, no! Ricardo, no!

5
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:40,708
IF EVERYONE WAS MURDERED,

6
00:00:40,791 --> 00:00:44,625
WHO WILL TELL THE STORY?

7
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:48,583
THE MURDERER?

8
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,291
No, no, no.

9
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:53,750
Oh, no!

10
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,041
What happened?

11
00:00:56,125 --> 00:00:58,750
-Come here!
-Shut the door!

12
00:00:58,833 --> 00:00:59,750
Dad!

13
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:00,708
Dad!

14
00:01:00,791 --> 00:01:01,708
Dad!

15
00:01:01,791 --> 00:01:02,875
Ricardo!

16
00:01:03,666 --> 00:01:06,041
-No, no!
-No, Ricardo!

17
00:01:06,125 --> 00:01:07,958
It's outside!

18
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:09,458
There it is.

19
00:01:09,541 --> 00:01:10,833
Get it.

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,333
Careful with the lampshades, Ricardo!

21
00:01:16,416 --> 00:01:17,625
That's enough.

22
00:01:20,041 --> 00:01:21,083
Is it dead?

23
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:23,666
Is it done?

24
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:26,708
Poor thing.

25
00:01:31,625 --> 00:01:33,166
We christened the house.

26
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:43,125
BARREDA: HUSBAND, FATHER, MURDERER

27
00:01:45,458 --> 00:01:46,916
-Barreda.
-Barreda, please.

28
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,333
A photo over here, Barreda.

29
00:01:48,416 --> 00:01:50,458
-Silence, please.
-Ricardo, look at the camera.

30
00:01:50,541 --> 00:01:51,541
Good morning.

31
00:01:52,208 --> 00:01:56,875
Let's proceed with the oral hearing
in the case against Mr. Ricardo Barreda.

32
00:01:57,583 --> 00:01:59,041
Over here, Doctor.

33
00:01:59,125 --> 00:02:01,833
Can the photographers
leave the room, please?

34
00:02:01,916 --> 00:02:03,083
Barreda.

35
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:06,833
Can you dim the lights, please? Thank you.

36
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:14,875
On November 15, 1992,

37
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:19,958
in the house located on 80948th Street
in La Plata,

38
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:25,583
its residents Gladys McDonald,
Cecilia and Adriana Barreda,

39
00:02:26,458 --> 00:02:29,750
and Elena Arreche
received multiple gunshots

40
00:02:30,625 --> 00:02:35,750
fired from a Victor Sarasqueta shotgun.

41
00:02:38,208 --> 00:02:42,416
Barreda, what did you do that day
after you killed them?

42
00:03:18,666 --> 00:03:20,375
Good morning, Barreda!

43
00:03:21,708 --> 00:03:22,708
Good morning.

44
00:03:26,041 --> 00:03:27,916
I'm sorry. He's looking for his friend.

45
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,500
Come on, boy.

46
00:03:29,583 --> 00:03:31,291
Yes, I'll let you know when I walk him.

47
00:03:31,375 --> 00:03:32,500
Say hi to Beba.

48
00:04:19,416 --> 00:04:20,833
What did you do, Barreda?

49
00:04:22,416 --> 00:04:23,625
I fucked up.

50
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:31,416
Leave it to me.

51
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:34,166
I'll handle it.

52
00:04:42,291 --> 00:04:45,833
LIVE BAIT
WE HAVE SHAD

53
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:46,916
You've really made me wait for you, love.

54
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,958
Yeah, I've made you wait.

55
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:15,541
Miss.

56
00:06:17,750 --> 00:06:19,041
Yes, tell me.

57
00:06:19,125 --> 00:06:21,083
-May I have another one of these?
-Sure.

58
00:06:26,833 --> 00:06:30,625
ROMA
PIZZA PLACE

59
00:06:53,458 --> 00:06:54,916
<i>No peeking.</i>

60
00:06:56,125 --> 00:06:57,250
<i>No peeking.</i>

61
00:07:01,458 --> 00:07:03,041
-Wait, it won't play it.
-So?

62
00:07:03,125 --> 00:07:04,666
-What's the surprise?
-There.

63
00:07:05,291 --> 00:07:07,291
The boom box you wanted.

64
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,500
It's for all of us to share.

65
00:07:10,583 --> 00:07:12,125
<i>When you think about someone</i>

66
00:07:12,208 --> 00:07:13,791
Oh, I see.

67
00:07:13,875 --> 00:07:15,375
It comes with a show.

68
00:07:15,458 --> 00:07:18,375
Here, this is for you. Merry Christmas.

69
00:07:19,666 --> 00:07:20,750
I made it myself.

70
00:07:21,416 --> 00:07:23,583
<i>When you are in the dark</i>

71
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:24,791
That's nice.

72
00:07:24,875 --> 00:07:26,208
I'm glad you like it.

73
00:07:28,375 --> 00:07:30,875
<i>When the morning comes</i>

74
00:07:32,083 --> 00:07:34,666
<i>You can see the sky and the world</i>

75
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:36,875
Hey! Will you come already?

76
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:38,708
Oh, wow!

77
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:40,708
I love it.

78
00:07:40,791 --> 00:07:42,708
It's beautiful.

79
00:07:42,791 --> 00:07:44,541
-This is great, Mom.
-Do you like it?

80
00:07:44,625 --> 00:07:46,833
-That's the one you wanted.
-Yes.

81
00:07:46,916 --> 00:07:48,125
It's beautiful.

82
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:50,833
They're high rise.
Will my butt fit in these?

83
00:07:50,916 --> 00:07:53,583
-That remains to be seen.
-You're so mean.

84
00:07:53,666 --> 00:07:56,041
Show Grandma. She pitched in.

85
00:07:56,125 --> 00:07:57,166
I love it.

86
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,250
-Thanks, Dad.
-Thanks.

87
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:01,875
This is for you.
I didn't forget what you wanted.

88
00:08:01,958 --> 00:08:04,416
You can't say I don't keep you in mind.

89
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:05,375
Thanks.

90
00:08:05,458 --> 00:08:07,375
Okay, girls. I have presents.

91
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:10,958
Grandma's full of bags
from El Corte Inglés.

92
00:08:11,041 --> 00:08:15,500
-This is for you, and this is for you.
-Is that what I think it is?

93
00:08:15,583 --> 00:08:17,958
Maybe. Open it.

94
00:08:18,041 --> 00:08:19,875
-Here, buy yourself something nice.
-Mom...

95
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:21,583
Come on, take it.

96
00:08:21,666 --> 00:08:24,625
-I didn't get you anything.
-Buy yourself whatever you want.

97
00:08:24,708 --> 00:08:26,416
Grandma!

98
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:30,416
Thanks, Mom.

99
00:08:31,208 --> 00:08:33,208
I bought it where you told me.

100
00:08:34,166 --> 00:08:37,083
The mannequin that was carrying it
commanded such authority

101
00:08:37,166 --> 00:08:38,541
that I almost fell in love.

102
00:08:38,625 --> 00:08:41,333
But I didn't buy you any cartridges.

103
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:42,416
-No.
-What?

104
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:45,125
It's for the best.
They say guns are loaded by the devil.

105
00:08:45,208 --> 00:08:48,291
Customs was a mess. There was a long line.

106
00:08:48,375 --> 00:08:50,708
But they saw I was an old lady
and let me go through.

107
00:08:50,791 --> 00:08:52,250
I could have smuggled drugs.

108
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:55,875
-How much did you drink?
-What you gave me.

109
00:08:55,958 --> 00:08:57,958
You haven't offered us anything yet, Mom.

110
00:08:58,041 --> 00:08:59,875
-I love it.
-Can I change it?

111
00:08:59,958 --> 00:09:01,250
-So nice.
-Yes.

112
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:02,875
No...

113
00:09:02,958 --> 00:09:06,625
Ricardo, go check
if the circuit breakers tripped.

114
00:09:34,916 --> 00:09:36,583
<i>Police station. Good evening.</i>

115
00:09:36,666 --> 00:09:39,541
Hello. Some robbers broke into my house.

116
00:09:39,625 --> 00:09:41,041
There are four bodies.

117
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:42,458
<i>Are you okay?</i>

118
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:46,916
Yes, I just got home and saw dead bodies.

119
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:15,875
-Let's go.
-This way.

120
00:10:28,666 --> 00:10:29,750
Commissioner.

121
00:10:34,625 --> 00:10:35,750
My God.

122
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:37,083
No signs of struggle.

123
00:10:37,166 --> 00:10:38,833
She didn't try to defend herself.

124
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:52,208
-Gentlemen.
-Good evening, Commissioner.

125
00:10:57,416 --> 00:10:59,041
Good evening, Commissioner.

126
00:11:04,791 --> 00:11:07,416
Commissioner, come with me, please.

127
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,500
Upstairs.

128
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,041
Weird, isn't it?

129
00:11:36,791 --> 00:11:38,541
They ransacked every room but this one.

130
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,541
Commissioner.

131
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:49,416
Who does that belong to?

132
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:52,750
It belonged to her.

133
00:11:55,666 --> 00:11:57,041
Excuse me, Barreda.

134
00:11:57,958 --> 00:12:00,458
-Can I address you informally?
-Yes.

135
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:03,625
You'll have to come with us
to the station.

136
00:12:05,250 --> 00:12:07,416
-What for?
-It's a routine procedure.

137
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,916
We won't keep you long.

138
00:12:09,541 --> 00:12:11,083
Gentlemen.

139
00:12:13,416 --> 00:12:16,291
Imagine losing your whole family.
I can't believe it.

140
00:12:16,375 --> 00:12:19,083
I took my dog out for a walk today
and everything seemed fine.

141
00:12:20,041 --> 00:12:21,916
Make way, please.

142
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,750
My deepest condolences, Barreda.

143
00:12:27,583 --> 00:12:29,916
How can you guarantee
this won't happen to me?

144
00:12:34,416 --> 00:12:37,583
-Come on!
-These are too big for me.

145
00:12:40,750 --> 00:12:42,291
-So?
-Yes.

146
00:12:43,125 --> 00:12:46,000
-No, these shoes are too big.
-Try the pink ones.

147
00:12:46,083 --> 00:12:49,958
-You can't get your diploma in flip-flops.
-I know, but I need low heels.

148
00:12:50,041 --> 00:12:51,958
-Something a bit more comfortable.
-Yes.

149
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,500
This looks weird.

150
00:12:54,583 --> 00:12:56,875
Yes, you need more boobs.

151
00:12:56,958 --> 00:12:59,500
Look who's talking.
You're not exactly Cicciolina.

152
00:12:59,583 --> 00:13:01,875
Hang on, I got it.

153
00:13:08,666 --> 00:13:10,750
-Be careful. Poor thing.
-Yes.

154
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:12,875
Let's see...

155
00:13:14,416 --> 00:13:16,791
Look at you. You're a bombshell.

156
00:13:17,583 --> 00:13:20,250
No, I look ridiculous.

157
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:22,625
Gastón will laugh at me
if he sees me like this.

158
00:13:22,708 --> 00:13:24,375
Did you tell Mom?

159
00:13:24,458 --> 00:13:25,708
No, not yet.

160
00:13:26,541 --> 00:13:27,916
Mommy!

161
00:13:28,750 --> 00:13:29,833
There we go.

162
00:13:31,916 --> 00:13:33,958
You can close your mouth now.

163
00:13:35,625 --> 00:13:37,375
The worst part is over.

164
00:13:39,333 --> 00:13:40,666
Did it hurt that much?

165
00:13:41,291 --> 00:13:43,208
I won't forgive myself for that.

166
00:13:43,916 --> 00:13:45,166
Do you know why?

167
00:13:45,958 --> 00:13:49,833
Because if it hurts,
it means I failed as a dentist.

168
00:13:52,791 --> 00:13:56,416
You know how your father gets.
Don't even think about telling him.

169
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,250
Okay, you're right.

170
00:13:58,333 --> 00:14:01,708
Later, if things work out
between you and this guy,

171
00:14:01,791 --> 00:14:05,958
we invite him over for some tea,
and you can introduce him formally.

172
00:14:06,041 --> 00:14:08,208
-But she already invited him.
-Stop, Adriana.

173
00:14:08,291 --> 00:14:10,666
-What?
-Are you two serious about each other?

174
00:14:13,333 --> 00:14:14,541
Ceci.

175
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:18,250
Yes.

176
00:14:19,166 --> 00:14:20,500
We're moving in together.

177
00:14:22,583 --> 00:14:23,750
And you're telling me now?

178
00:14:24,708 --> 00:14:25,833
I'm sorry.

179
00:14:25,916 --> 00:14:26,916
Does he have a family?

180
00:14:27,708 --> 00:14:28,875
Yes, he has a daughter.

181
00:14:28,958 --> 00:14:29,958
He's great.

182
00:14:31,208 --> 00:14:33,833
-Oh, no, Cecilia.
-We're serious, Mom.

183
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:36,791
What were you talking about?

184
00:14:36,875 --> 00:14:38,666
You look so fancy, Grandma.

185
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:39,916
-Really?
-Yes.

186
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,625
-Do you like it?
-Yes.

187
00:14:41,708 --> 00:14:42,958
Is that what you're wearing?

188
00:14:43,666 --> 00:14:45,583
Yes. Why? I don't look good in it?

189
00:14:46,416 --> 00:14:48,291
No, it's beautiful.

190
00:14:51,750 --> 00:14:52,833
Almost...

191
00:14:55,291 --> 00:14:57,083
There we go.

192
00:14:58,458 --> 00:15:02,041
So, has anyone
ever treated you this nicely?

193
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,125
Spit in there.

194
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:12,375
What is it?

195
00:15:13,541 --> 00:15:16,083
-We're ready.
-Wait for me outside.

196
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:18,208
Okay.

197
00:15:19,833 --> 00:15:20,708
Family.

198
00:15:20,791 --> 00:15:22,916
-Has anyone seen the keys?
-No, not me.

199
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,666
-Hello.
-Commissioner.

200
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:31,666
How does he look? Has he eaten?

201
00:15:31,750 --> 00:15:33,125
No, but he's calm.

202
00:15:33,208 --> 00:15:37,041
{\an8}Bring him some food. Make conversation,
give him a little distraction.

203
00:15:37,125 --> 00:15:38,708
{\an8}MONZÓN
WORLD CHAMPION - NATIONAL IDOL

204
00:16:02,291 --> 00:16:03,291
Help yourself.

205
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,375
-Thanks.
-No problem.

206
00:16:07,208 --> 00:16:08,250
Excuse me.

207
00:16:17,375 --> 00:16:18,500
{\an8}Do you like the champ?

208
00:16:19,791 --> 00:16:24,625
That was taken in 1970,
when he beat Benvenuti in Rome.

209
00:16:24,708 --> 00:16:28,250
-Well, well, we have a fan.
-The number one fan.

210
00:16:28,333 --> 00:16:31,458
-Did you ever meet him?
-I saw him a couple of times at Atenas.

211
00:16:32,875 --> 00:16:33,916
Did you talk to him?

212
00:16:35,583 --> 00:16:38,625
I must have asked him, "What's up, champ?"

213
00:16:39,458 --> 00:16:40,833
"How are you doing?"

214
00:16:41,708 --> 00:16:43,125
Unfortunately...

215
00:16:44,166 --> 00:16:47,541
fame and his issues with women
took him on another path.

216
00:16:55,291 --> 00:16:57,250
We'll have to see each other again.

217
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,333
You have to complete
the treatment in one week.

218
00:17:01,083 --> 00:17:02,541
Don't give me that look.

219
00:17:03,208 --> 00:17:05,000
It didn't hurt that much, did it?

220
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:06,791
No, don't touch it.

221
00:17:07,708 --> 00:17:12,250
Apply some ice for the swelling
and don't do any workout.

222
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:13,750
None at all, okay?

223
00:17:14,416 --> 00:17:15,333
Where's your purse?

224
00:17:15,416 --> 00:17:18,666
Whatever you need, call me.
Or I'll call you.

225
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:20,875
-Thanks, Doctor.
-Of course.

226
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:25,583
The four of you are on time.
It's a miracle.

227
00:17:25,666 --> 00:17:26,833
Don't start, Ricardo.

228
00:17:32,541 --> 00:17:35,583
Mom, come here.
Don't you want to sit at the front?

229
00:17:42,541 --> 00:17:45,666
Guys, you can leave now, please.

230
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:56,750
The <i>Criminal Code.</i>

231
00:18:02,625 --> 00:18:04,750
I found a way to get you out of this.

232
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,208
We can cite psychiatric problems.

233
00:18:07,291 --> 00:18:08,625
Psychiatric?

234
00:18:09,291 --> 00:18:10,458
Look.

235
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:14,083
Read this.

236
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
"Section 34."

237
00:18:22,708 --> 00:18:28,166
"It's not punishable
if during the incident,

238
00:18:28,250 --> 00:18:32,000
the person could not control their actions
in case of alienation..."

239
00:18:32,083 --> 00:18:33,708
But I didn't do anything.

240
00:18:35,875 --> 00:18:38,291
You took
a criminology course recently, right?

241
00:18:39,333 --> 00:18:41,666
At the bar association, remember?

242
00:18:44,291 --> 00:18:46,000
How did you know that?

243
00:18:47,666 --> 00:18:49,125
This is a small city.

244
00:18:50,958 --> 00:18:54,583
Look, I won't turn you in,
but I need you to cooperate.

245
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:57,750
Let's do the following.

246
00:18:58,375 --> 00:19:00,625
You'll tell me where you hid the gun,

247
00:19:00,708 --> 00:19:02,750
and I'll tell you
who told me about the course.

248
00:19:03,916 --> 00:19:06,750
If you cooperate and do as I say,
you'll get out of this one.

249
00:19:11,583 --> 00:19:13,041
Where's the gun?

250
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:26,333
In Punta Lara.

251
00:19:26,416 --> 00:19:31,666
I ran into Patricia Hernández
and I asked her about the wedding.

252
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:33,291
-If she was coming...
-One second.

253
00:19:33,375 --> 00:19:36,333
-Can you lower the volume so I can hear?
-Yes, Dad.

254
00:19:37,875 --> 00:19:38,875
Okay. Keep going.

255
00:19:38,958 --> 00:19:41,333
-There's something fishy there.
-Yes.

256
00:19:41,416 --> 00:19:44,166
Yes, I think she has
a problem with her father.

257
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:46,000
He has a betting problem.

258
00:19:46,083 --> 00:19:48,083
-A gambling issue?
-That's awful.

259
00:19:48,166 --> 00:19:51,958
Either way, you can't torment your family
because of your addiction.

260
00:19:52,666 --> 00:19:56,333
Carlos paid good money
to fix her wife's teeth.

261
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,916
