507
00:35:56,375 --> 00:35:59,750
According to other witnesses,
you and Cecilia were very close.

508
00:36:00,458 --> 00:36:04,416
So, why wouldn't you go
to her house more often?

509
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,500
It was awkward.

510
00:36:08,625 --> 00:36:10,791
He behaved in a weird way towards us.

511
00:36:10,875 --> 00:36:12,000
In what way?

512
00:36:13,041 --> 00:36:14,250
He...

513
00:36:17,750 --> 00:36:19,125
He would stare at us.

514
00:36:19,708 --> 00:36:21,000
He stared at you.

515
00:36:21,750 --> 00:36:25,083
-You mean... in a lascivious way?
-Objection.

516
00:36:25,166 --> 00:36:27,208
It's a suggestive question.

517
00:36:27,291 --> 00:36:28,541
Sustained.

518
00:36:28,625 --> 00:36:31,083
Counselor, please rephrase the question.

519
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:35,875
How did Mr. Barreda
look at you and your friends?

520
00:36:37,416 --> 00:36:39,083
The way men look at women.

521
00:36:39,916 --> 00:36:41,041
He looked at our legs.

522
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:43,000
Everywhere.

523
00:36:43,750 --> 00:36:45,875
Other friends would say the same thing.

524
00:36:46,500 --> 00:36:48,750
Cecilia and Adriana
would get very uncomfortable.

525
00:36:49,500 --> 00:36:51,250
Why do you think that is?

526
00:36:52,750 --> 00:36:56,000
They were affected by the things
he did outside his home.

527
00:36:56,625 --> 00:36:59,666
Once, Cecilia, my boyfriend and I
were at the Jockey Club.

528
00:37:00,625 --> 00:37:02,791
And he arrived at the pool with a woman.

529
00:37:03,833 --> 00:37:06,666
We tried to distract Cecilia
so she wouldn't see him,

530
00:37:06,750 --> 00:37:08,666
but Ceci wasn't stupid.

531
00:37:08,750 --> 00:37:10,666
These things affected her.

532
00:37:11,625 --> 00:37:15,041
That's why I think she didn't have
much of a relationship with her father.

533
00:37:39,416 --> 00:37:40,416
Dad.

534
00:37:41,875 --> 00:37:45,791
Dad, leave it. I'll pick it up later.
I'll wash this first.

535
00:37:49,833 --> 00:37:51,750
What was your daily routine at home?

536
00:37:55,541 --> 00:38:00,583
I worked all day in my office,

537
00:38:01,291 --> 00:38:06,000
and when I finished,
I would do all the household chores.

538
00:38:07,791 --> 00:38:10,875
They were very dirty.

539
00:38:11,708 --> 00:38:15,416
And messy.
They left everything disorganized.

540
00:38:16,416 --> 00:38:20,166
And they knew I was very clean,
very meticulous.

541
00:38:21,041 --> 00:38:23,250
Sometimes, one of my daughters

542
00:38:24,083 --> 00:38:26,916
would try to help me,
but they would stop them.

543
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,166
Who stopped them?

544
00:38:28,250 --> 00:38:30,083
They wouldn't let them.

545
00:38:31,250 --> 00:38:36,125
"Leave it like that.
Pussy can take care of it," they said.

546
00:38:48,125 --> 00:38:50,125
But I was worried.

547
00:38:50,208 --> 00:38:52,750
-But why, Grandma?
-Because I saw him drinking a lot.

548
00:38:53,500 --> 00:38:56,791
I thought he was a minor. What a mess.

549
00:38:56,875 --> 00:39:00,083
-He's like 25, Grandma.
-Okay, sweetie.

550
00:39:00,166 --> 00:39:01,791
Then, he's a little man.

551
00:39:01,875 --> 00:39:03,208
Not at all.

552
00:39:03,291 --> 00:39:07,708
-He usually gets nervous, that's all.
-He's a funny little man.

553
00:39:07,791 --> 00:39:11,083
Martín says he does it because he has
an inferiority complex.

554
00:39:11,166 --> 00:39:13,333
-I'll read yours, Grandma.
-Sure, go ahead.

555
00:39:13,416 --> 00:39:18,958
"Dynamic week, though rather tense.
Change is coming. You must be alert."

556
00:39:19,041 --> 00:39:20,958
-I must be alert?
-Yes.

557
00:39:21,041 --> 00:39:26,791
"You sometimes act with aggressiveness,
and he hates that."

558
00:39:26,875 --> 00:39:29,583
-Who's "he"?
-The little man.

559
00:39:29,666 --> 00:39:33,583
-The cardiologist.
-The little cardiologist.

560
00:39:33,666 --> 00:39:36,875
The cardiologist isn't a little man.
He's very handsome.

561
00:39:37,958 --> 00:39:41,791
They did everything behind my back.

562
00:39:43,875 --> 00:39:47,291
And I had to pay for all their whims,

563
00:39:47,375 --> 00:39:51,166
otherwise they would start insulting me,

564
00:39:52,083 --> 00:39:53,333
and threatening me.

565
00:39:54,125 --> 00:39:56,000
Your daughters, too?

566
00:39:56,625 --> 00:39:57,708
Them, too.

567
00:39:58,708 --> 00:40:00,458
It was all my mother-in-law's fault.

568
00:40:01,166 --> 00:40:04,833
She was the mastermind
behind my family's ruin.

569
00:40:06,708 --> 00:40:10,000
If the abuse was so great,
why didn't you leave?

570
00:40:14,125 --> 00:40:18,000
Because I wanted to get my family back.

571
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,000
That's why I bought the house.

572
00:40:22,916 --> 00:40:24,708
I wanted a family.

573
00:40:25,666 --> 00:40:28,000
Thanks. No more questions.

574
00:40:39,375 --> 00:40:43,958
<i>As you can see, this is
the atmosphere outside the courthouse.</i>

575
00:40:44,041 --> 00:40:46,500
<i>What do you think
about Barreda in this case?</i>

576
00:40:46,583 --> 00:40:49,458
<i>I understand him. I went through the same
and I didn't speak up.</i>

577
00:40:49,541 --> 00:40:51,666
<i>I know what it's like
for a woman to ruin you.</i>

578
00:40:51,750 --> 00:40:54,166
Go, Barreda! You're amazing!

579
00:40:54,250 --> 00:40:55,375
We're with you!

580
00:40:57,208 --> 00:40:59,250
Go, Pussy!

581
00:41:00,375 --> 00:41:03,291
Look, there's some air in there.

582
00:41:03,375 --> 00:41:06,500
You have to make sure it's neat
and that it matches the rest,

583
00:41:07,791 --> 00:41:09,375
-because that will last forever.
-Yes

584
00:41:15,250 --> 00:41:17,708
What's that stain? Is that dry?

585
00:41:18,666 --> 00:41:21,333
Yes, it's dry.
You won't notice after we paint over it.

586
00:41:21,416 --> 00:41:25,291
How long do you think it will take
for you to wallpaper everything?

587
00:41:27,208 --> 00:41:29,916
A week, a week and a half.

588
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:32,583
I'll bring my team,
and we'll do it in no time.

589
00:41:32,666 --> 00:41:36,708
Okay. Can you check this defective
electrical outlet before you leave?

590
00:41:36,791 --> 00:41:39,625
-Yes, ma'am.
-Thank you.

591
00:41:39,708 --> 00:41:41,416
We're not very handy.

592
00:41:45,500 --> 00:41:47,083
Mom, can you hand me the towel?

593
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,208
Mom.

594
00:41:57,708 --> 00:42:00,375
Thanks. The faucet won't close properly.

595
00:42:01,791 --> 00:42:03,041
Leave it like that.

596
00:42:03,125 --> 00:42:05,666
-Should I tell Dad?
-No, don't say anything.

597
00:42:06,750 --> 00:42:09,791
Please set the table so we can eat
as soon as your sister is here.

598
00:42:15,833 --> 00:42:17,666
Mom, you can't keep living this way.

599
00:42:18,791 --> 00:42:21,416
Maybe you should talk to someone.

600
00:42:22,041 --> 00:42:24,208
Why don't you call Lucía's mom?

601
00:42:24,291 --> 00:42:25,458
A psychologist?

602
00:42:26,791 --> 00:42:28,541
Rather, I should call a lawyer...

603
00:42:28,625 --> 00:42:30,708
-Oh, Mom.
-No, I don't think so.

604
00:42:30,791 --> 00:42:33,208
I'm not going to talk
about our private life.

605
00:42:33,291 --> 00:42:35,125
To a stranger?

606
00:42:36,291 --> 00:42:38,375
You're adults now, and you'll leave soon.

607
00:42:38,958 --> 00:42:40,208
I'll sort things out.

608
00:42:54,958 --> 00:42:56,916
How did the interview go?

609
00:42:58,375 --> 00:42:59,375
What?

610
00:43:01,458 --> 00:43:03,916
Fine. Well, who knows?

611
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:07,583
They haven't called me yet,
but Claudia said it takes a while.

612
00:43:07,666 --> 00:43:10,166
-That's true.
-Is that faucet still leaking?

613
00:43:11,416 --> 00:43:14,291
My head's about to explode.

614
00:43:14,375 --> 00:43:17,208
-Hello.
-Hi.

615
00:43:17,291 --> 00:43:20,250
-What did you do to your hair?
-It's a new look. You like it?

616
00:43:20,333 --> 00:43:23,208
-Yes, I like it.
-Why did you do that?

617
00:43:23,291 --> 00:43:25,000
-Mom.
-I did the same thing at your age.

618
00:43:25,083 --> 00:43:26,625
Yes, you're a copycat.

619
00:43:26,708 --> 00:43:29,208
-But it looks beautiful now.
-Yes.

620
00:43:29,291 --> 00:43:33,416
This happens because you open
and close it all the time.

621
00:43:33,500 --> 00:43:37,541
That's because it's a faucet, Ricardo.
Leave it, we already called a plumber.

622
00:43:37,625 --> 00:43:39,000
Sure you did.

623
00:43:39,666 --> 00:43:42,500
-Girls, can you set the table?
-Sure.

624
00:43:42,583 --> 00:43:44,916
Ricardo, turn it off!

625
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:46,875
Dad, turn off the tap!

626
00:43:46,958 --> 00:43:48,750
Turn it off, Ricardo!

627
00:43:48,833 --> 00:43:51,833
I got it. I turned off the main valve.

628
00:43:53,750 --> 00:43:56,958
Mom, you're soaked! And you too!

629
00:43:58,875 --> 00:44:01,166
Quiet, he'll get upset.

630
00:44:01,250 --> 00:44:04,916
Who cares? He can't fix anything!

631
00:44:07,500 --> 00:44:08,583
Barreda.

632
00:44:10,916 --> 00:44:12,250
Come in.

633
00:44:18,958 --> 00:44:20,166
Jeez.

634
00:44:22,958 --> 00:44:24,250
You look awful.

635
00:44:24,333 --> 00:44:27,833
I feel pain here. In this area, yes.

636
00:44:30,458 --> 00:44:32,791
-Sit. I'll be right back.
-Okay.

637
00:44:43,500 --> 00:44:45,250
Someone cast the evil eye on you.

638
00:44:58,458 --> 00:45:00,208
-What should I do?
-Cut the deck.

639
00:45:13,583 --> 00:45:14,875
I'm not doing well.

640
00:45:16,583 --> 00:45:19,041
I feel like an idiot, everything hurts.

641
00:45:22,750 --> 00:45:23,791
Look.

642
00:45:24,875 --> 00:45:26,083
Your house.

643
00:45:26,875 --> 00:45:27,916
What?

644
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:30,166
You've been bewitched.

645
00:45:30,916 --> 00:45:32,000
What?

646
00:45:33,333 --> 00:45:34,333
Look.

647
00:45:34,416 --> 00:45:36,083
The real question is "who."

648
00:45:36,958 --> 00:45:37,958
Who?

649
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:41,875
These women did something to you.

650
00:45:43,375 --> 00:45:44,708
Search your house.

651
00:45:45,791 --> 00:45:48,666
Search well. You'll be surprised.

652
00:45:49,583 --> 00:45:51,000
Grab another one.

653
00:45:57,458 --> 00:46:00,333
Introduce yourself to the court, please.

654
00:46:00,416 --> 00:46:03,375
Tell us your name, occupation,
and relationship to the defendant.

655
00:46:04,375 --> 00:46:09,666
My name is María de los Ángeles Arba,
but everyone has always called me Pirucha.

656
00:46:10,583 --> 00:46:13,458
I'm a clairvoyant and Barreda's friend.

657
00:46:14,125 --> 00:46:15,750
And his lover, right?

658
00:46:16,750 --> 00:46:18,791
I'd say a very close friend.

659
00:46:18,875 --> 00:46:21,750
But above all else,
I'm his spiritual guide.

660
00:46:23,166 --> 00:46:25,583
Did Barreda tell you about his life?

661
00:46:25,666 --> 00:46:27,125
He did.

662
00:46:28,166 --> 00:46:31,500
And what he didn't tell me,
I would know anyway.

663
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:37,541
So, I imagine you knew
about his problems with the house.

664
00:46:38,416 --> 00:46:40,250
His house? I don't get it.

665
00:46:40,333 --> 00:46:43,041
Well, Barreda didn't want
to sell the house.

666
00:46:43,125 --> 00:46:45,500
He wanted to keep it.
Didn't he mention that?

667
00:46:45,583 --> 00:46:47,416
Objection. Suggestive question.

668
00:46:47,500 --> 00:46:48,750
Sustained.

669
00:46:48,833 --> 00:46:51,208
Counselor, please rephrase the question.

670
00:46:53,291 --> 00:46:56,375
How did Barreda look to you lately?

671
00:46:57,291 --> 00:46:58,375
Bad.

672
00:46:59,166 --> 00:47:00,625
-Very bad.
-You mean aggressive.

673
00:47:00,708 --> 00:47:03,333
-Objection.
-Counselor.

674
00:47:06,291 --> 00:47:09,000
Please, tell us why he looked bad to you.

675
00:47:09,083 --> 00:47:12,666
Barreda was going through...

676
00:47:13,250 --> 00:47:16,916
a very confusing and a very dark time.

677
00:47:18,416 --> 00:47:21,750
His body had been bewitched.

678
00:47:22,541 --> 00:47:24,625
No more questions. Thank you.

679
00:47:26,708 --> 00:47:30,041
-You're so handy.
-Thank you.

680
00:47:30,125 --> 00:47:32,041
So embarrassing. We're making you work.

681
00:47:32,125 --> 00:47:35,250
No, it's nothing.
I was taught when I was little.

682
00:47:37,666 --> 00:47:40,125
Do you want more tea, guys?
You should eat something.

683
00:47:40,208 --> 00:47:42,041
You didn't even touch the snacks.

684
00:47:43,250 --> 00:47:44,666
-I'll try some.
-Yes.

685
00:47:44,750 --> 00:47:46,625
I'm good. Thanks.

686
00:47:46,708 --> 00:47:49,208
-Okay, I'll get you some.
-Thanks.

687
00:47:51,458 --> 00:47:55,041
-So you know the Blancos's youngest son?
-Yes, Luisito.

688
00:47:55,125 --> 00:47:56,250
Shorty!

689
00:47:57,750 --> 00:48:00,333
Half a man, a tiny man. He's little.

690
00:48:00,416 --> 00:48:02,166
-Yes.
-That's what they call him.

691
00:48:02,250 --> 00:48:03,708
-"Sissy."
-Come on.

692
00:48:03,791 --> 00:48:05,833
I don't like it when they call him that.

693
00:48:05,916 --> 00:48:08,958
I don't like it either,
but compared to other men...

694
00:48:09,041 --> 00:48:11,250
-Yes, he's effeminate.
-Yes.

695
00:48:12,458 --> 00:48:16,041
Good afternoon.
Nice to meet you. I'm Gastón.

696
00:48:16,125 --> 00:48:18,166
-Gastón?
-He's my boyfriend.

697
00:48:18,250 --> 00:48:21,875
-Yes.
-Are you a plumber?

698
00:48:22,458 --> 00:48:26,458
No, but I like to fix stuff.
Actually, I'm a PE teacher at Lincoln.

699
00:48:26,541 --> 00:48:29,875
You're being modest.
He's in charge of the other teachers.

700
00:48:29,958 --> 00:48:31,708
That's amazing.

701
00:48:32,541 --> 00:48:35,291
-You also have a position at the club.
-Really? What club?

702
00:48:35,375 --> 00:48:38,291
We're looking for a venue
for their wedding.

703
00:48:38,375 --> 00:48:40,500
We saw several venues,
but didn't like any.

704
00:48:40,583 --> 00:48:41,583
What about the Rotary?

705
00:48:41,666 --> 00:48:44,791
-Okay, this is working fine now.
-You're an angel.

706
00:48:45,666 --> 00:48:47,583
It's so nice to have a handyman.

707
00:48:47,666 --> 00:48:49,500
Looks like you're the girl here.

708
00:48:51,083 --> 00:48:52,333
What did you say?

709
00:48:52,416 --> 00:48:54,625
I said,
looks like our girl here is leaving.

710
00:48:54,708 --> 00:48:56,916
Well, not for a while, Baba.

711
00:48:57,000 --> 00:49:00,000
As soon as Ceci gets
her residency training.

712
00:49:00,083 --> 00:49:03,208
Is that so? And where will you move?

713
00:49:03,875 --> 00:49:05,250
It depends on the hospital.

714
00:49:06,000 --> 00:49:09,875
I hope it's here,
but it could be in the capital, too.

715
00:49:09,958 --> 00:49:13,291
And that would be closer for us
to go see Sofi on the weekends.

716
00:49:14,416 --> 00:49:15,333
Well...

717
00:49:15,416 --> 00:49:17,625
-How old is your daughter?
-Six.

718
00:49:17,708 --> 00:49:19,000
-Six.
-She's in first grade.

719
00:49:19,083 --> 00:49:22,250
-So nice.
-Yes, he has a daughter.

720
00:49:23,375 --> 00:49:27,166
That's nice. So many news.

721
00:49:28,208 --> 00:49:31,041
That's a nice toolbox you've got.
It has everything.

722
00:49:32,625 --> 00:49:33,958
Excuse me.

723
00:49:39,083 --> 00:49:41,166
Well, shall I put the kettle on?

724
00:49:42,875 --> 00:49:45,500
Don't worry. It's not you.
He's like this with everyone.

725
00:49:45,583 --> 00:49:46,791
I understand. Poor man.

726
00:49:46,875 --> 00:49:50,291
I don't know what I'll do
when my daughter gets married and leaves.

727
00:49:58,166 --> 00:50:03,208
Everything he said
about the abuse is a lie.

728
00:50:04,333 --> 00:50:05,416
In fact,

729
00:50:06,833 --> 00:50:10,583
when I got the call,
I immediately thought,

730
00:50:12,875 --> 00:50:14,791
"That son of a bitch killed them."

731
00:50:15,750 --> 00:50:17,708
Please, watch your language.

732
00:50:18,583 --> 00:50:19,833
Go on, Counselor.

733
00:50:20,541 --> 00:50:21,750
Who are you talking about?

734
00:50:24,833 --> 00:50:25,875
Him.

735
00:50:27,541 --> 00:50:28,875
Mr. Barreda?

736
00:50:29,541 --> 00:50:30,625
Yes.

737
00:50:30,708 --> 00:50:35,000
Let it be on the record that the witness
pointed at Ricardo Barreda.

738
00:50:35,750 --> 00:50:39,291
In that moment, what made you so sure?

739
00:50:41,416 --> 00:50:43,250
He was a manipulative man.

740
00:50:44,916 --> 00:50:47,500
He'd make them feel bad all the time.

741
00:50:50,666 --> 00:50:52,708
He wasn't a normal father.

742
00:50:52,791 --> 00:50:55,083
I'm sure he had something against them.

743
00:50:56,500 --> 00:50:59,791
To your understanding,
why do you think he killed them?

744
00:51:02,125 --> 00:51:06,666
Because Ceci and I
were moving in together.

745
00:51:08,333 --> 00:51:10,583
Because Martín and Adri
were getting married.

746
00:51:12,250 --> 00:51:13,875
Because they were going to be happy.

747
00:51:15,916 --> 00:51:17,166
Because he's a bastard.

748
00:51:23,625 --> 00:51:25,958
That's all. Thanks.

749
00:51:26,750 --> 00:51:28,500
No more questions.

750
00:51:31,833 --> 00:51:35,250
-Be careful what you're about to say.
-I'd say either Gemini or Aquarius.

751
00:51:35,333 --> 00:51:36,333
Come on!

752
00:51:40,375 --> 00:51:42,416
Astrologers are all liars!

753
00:51:43,083 --> 00:51:44,916
Am I right?

754
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:47,333
The first astrologers
were the Three Wise Men.

755
00:51:47,916 --> 00:51:50,208
Yes, Melchior, Gaspar, and Balthasar.

756
00:51:50,291 --> 00:51:52,000
The Three Wise Men, she says.

757
00:51:52,083 --> 00:51:53,500
Party's over, I suppose.

758
00:51:54,750 --> 00:51:56,541
No, it's fine.

759
00:51:59,791 --> 00:52:01,041
Good night, Mom.

760
00:52:01,125 --> 00:52:02,750
Good night.

761
00:52:12,041 --> 00:52:14,500
-Ricardo, I went looking for you.
-Yes.

762
00:52:14,583 --> 00:52:18,083
How much longer is this guy going to stay?
Is he going to live here now?

763
00:52:18,166 --> 00:52:19,541
Stop that.

764
00:52:20,291 --> 00:52:22,375
It's so hard to live like this.

765
00:52:22,458 --> 00:52:25,791
-There's no communication between us.
-Us?

766
00:52:26,666 --> 00:52:29,000
You mean us two? Us three?

767
00:52:30,166 --> 00:52:32,083
How many is "us," Bebita?

768
00:52:33,250 --> 00:52:34,750
I'm not going to argue with you.

769
00:52:37,666 --> 00:52:38,916
Good night.

770
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:47,250
What happened now?

771
00:52:49,333 --> 00:52:51,250
Do you know why you suffer?

772
00:52:52,250 --> 00:52:56,458
You're still expecting him to change,
but he'll never change.

773
00:53:40,541 --> 00:53:42,250
-Go ahead.
-Thanks.

774
00:53:44,625 --> 00:53:46,708
Here you go, Doctor.

775
00:53:47,458 --> 00:53:48,583
Thanks.

776
00:54:02,458 --> 00:54:03,708
Bebi.

777
00:54:03,791 --> 00:54:04,791
Yes?

778
00:54:04,875 --> 00:54:08,250
Why don't you also try the shoes on?
It will look different.

779
00:54:10,666 --> 00:54:15,750
-There's no need.
-Bebi, look at you.

780
00:54:16,583 --> 00:54:19,375
Beautiful.

781
00:54:34,000 --> 00:54:35,500
You look gorgeous.

782
00:54:35,583 --> 00:54:38,625
I like it. I'd make it shorter, though.

783
00:54:38,708 --> 00:54:41,000
-Just a little?
-No. Don't.

784
00:54:41,083 --> 00:54:43,125
-Just a little bit.
-No, it's a wedding.

785
00:54:45,083 --> 00:54:46,125
So?

786
00:54:58,666 --> 00:55:01,666
-Do you like it?
-Yes, you look beautiful.

787
00:55:01,750 --> 00:55:03,958
-I love it.
-You look gorgeous.

788
00:55:04,041 --> 00:55:05,833
-Really?
-I love it.

789
00:55:05,916 --> 00:55:08,083
-I love the embroidery.
-It's got something here.

790
00:55:18,375 --> 00:55:20,000
It's too tight, Mom.

791
00:55:20,833 --> 00:55:22,583
-Here? Silvi...
-Yes.

792
00:55:22,666 --> 00:55:25,958
-Yes?
-Can you loosen it a little here?

793
00:55:26,041 --> 00:55:27,416
-You can attach a hook.
-Yes.

794
00:55:33,875 --> 00:55:36,541
You know what it's like to be
uncomfortable at your wedding?

795
00:55:36,625 --> 00:55:38,416
Wasn't your dress comfortable, Mom?

796
00:55:46,291 --> 00:55:49,916
It was so long ago. I don't remember.
It was Grandma's dress.

797
00:55:50,708 --> 00:55:52,666
We did some alterations and that was it.

798
00:55:56,875 --> 00:56:00,625
You have to be okay with it.
It's not just about a dress.

799
00:56:00,708 --> 00:56:05,166
Happiness is built from the outside in.

800
00:56:05,791 --> 00:56:07,625
-Right?
-I think it's the other way around.

801
00:56:15,208 --> 00:56:16,833
I'll get something for you hair.

802
00:56:17,916 --> 00:56:18,916
-Ready?
-Yes.

803
00:56:20,833 --> 00:56:24,083
-Adri, you wanted a dress like this one.
-Yes, but it's uncomfortable.

804
00:56:34,041 --> 00:56:35,708
-Ready?
-Yes.

805
00:56:35,791 --> 00:56:39,000
Adriana, you wanted to get married
in a white dress.

806
00:56:39,083 --> 00:56:40,750
You chose this dress.

807
00:56:41,333 --> 00:56:43,291
I didn't know it'd fit like this.

808
00:56:43,375 --> 00:56:48,208
<i>Did you ever witness the abuse
the defendant claims to have endured?</i>

809
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:52,083
Do you think it was real?

810
00:56:54,833 --> 00:56:56,000
No, I don't think so.

811
00:56:56,625 --> 00:56:59,750
They were a discreet family.
I never heard them yell at each other.

812
00:56:59,833 --> 00:57:03,625
That being said,
would you say the word "Pussy"

813
00:57:04,416 --> 00:57:08,416
is something that
could have been used frequently

814
00:57:08,500 --> 00:57:12,166
by Mrs. Gladys McDonald,
the defendant's wife?

815
00:57:14,583 --> 00:57:17,750
Beba? No way. She didn't curse.

816
00:57:20,041 --> 00:57:23,791
Well, we've established
that there was no abuse,

817
00:57:23,875 --> 00:57:27,166
and even if there was,
it doesn't justify the incident.

818
00:57:27,250 --> 00:57:29,708
Thank you. No more questions.

819
00:57:30,500 --> 00:57:31,750
Very well.

820
00:57:31,833 --> 00:57:34,708
-Does the defense have any questions?
-Yes, thank you.

821
00:57:38,458 --> 00:57:42,666
You said you knew Cecilia your whole life.

822
00:57:43,625 --> 00:57:47,000
Would you say the Barredas were well-off?

823
00:57:51,083 --> 00:57:53,833
I don't know the details,
but I think they were doing fine.

824
00:57:54,833 --> 00:58:00,708
Did Cecilia Barreda ever mention what was
the source of income in her family?

825
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:03,916
No, we didn't talk about that.

826
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:08,666
But I'm sure you can deduce
who was paying the household bills.

827
00:58:08,750 --> 00:58:10,166
Objection. That's not relevant.

828
00:58:10,250 --> 00:58:13,125
This isn't a child support trial,
it's a multiple homicide trial.

829
00:58:13,208 --> 00:58:15,750
Sustained. Get to the point, Counselor.

830
00:58:16,916 --> 00:58:17,916
Okay.

831
00:58:19,791 --> 00:58:21,916
How did Cecilia talk about her father?

832
00:58:23,625 --> 00:58:26,375
With admiration, with disdain?

833
00:58:28,250 --> 00:58:29,708
She didn't mention him much.

834
00:58:30,625 --> 00:58:34,458
So, can we say that Mr. Ricardo Barreda

835
00:58:34,541 --> 00:58:39,541
was always present when it came
to covering the family's expenses,

836
00:58:39,625 --> 00:58:43,291
but he didn't receive
any affection in return?

837
00:58:48,583 --> 00:58:51,416
-I don't know.
-No more questions. Thank you.

838
00:58:51,500 --> 00:58:53,708
The witness may leave. Thank you.

839
00:59:01,125 --> 00:59:02,541
Well, it seems to be going well.

840
00:59:57,375 --> 00:59:58,791
Operating room number three.

841
01:00:01,958 --> 01:00:03,458
Stay still.

842
01:01:00,958 --> 01:01:05,875
<i>The man I've known my whole life
would never even hurt a fly.</i>

843
01:01:07,041 --> 01:01:08,708
What changed in him, then?

844
01:01:08,791 --> 01:01:09,833
His spirit.

845
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:13,125
Barreda was possessed by a demonic force

846
01:01:13,208 --> 01:01:16,541
because those women
wanted to take everything for themselves,

847
01:01:16,625 --> 01:01:20,041
but since they couldn't,
they turned to black magic to kill him.

848
01:01:21,041 --> 01:01:23,000
What makes you so sure about that?

849
01:01:23,541 --> 01:01:26,583
It's my gift, sir. My visions.

850
01:01:27,500 --> 01:01:30,833
Sometimes, you see things,
but you don't talk about them.

851
01:01:31,916 --> 01:01:33,166
And the facts.

852
01:01:34,125 --> 01:01:36,291
He had all sorts of pain.

853
01:01:36,375 --> 01:01:39,458
The darkness was taking over his body,
and I'm not surprised.

854
01:01:40,166 --> 01:01:43,583
-Did Barreda believe in this stuff?
-Yes, of course.

855
01:01:44,250 --> 01:01:45,416
Don't you?

856
01:01:47,750 --> 01:01:49,125
He suffered.

857
01:01:49,208 --> 01:01:50,625
Men are weaker.

858
01:01:50,708 --> 01:01:55,291
With just one prick on a voodoo doll,
they come undone.

859
01:01:55,375 --> 01:01:56,666
Like flan.

860
01:02:01,500 --> 01:02:02,500
Voodoo doll?

861
01:02:03,750 --> 01:02:05,000
Yes. A voodoo doll.

862
01:02:06,250 --> 01:02:09,916
In fact, Barreda found it
and brought it to me.

863
01:02:14,375 --> 01:02:15,958
Silence, please.

864
01:02:18,708 --> 01:02:19,750
If I may.

865
01:02:20,291 --> 01:02:22,083
Will you hand me that, please?

866
01:02:26,166 --> 01:02:30,416
When you talk about a voodoo doll,
is this what you mean?

867
01:02:31,583 --> 01:02:33,708
That's what it looked like in my visions.

868
01:02:33,791 --> 01:02:35,375
What about the one Barreda found?

869
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:37,041
Like that one.

870
01:02:40,833 --> 01:02:44,375
This is a pin cushion I bought
this morning at a notions store.

871
01:02:45,083 --> 01:02:49,000
Probably Elena, who sewed once in a while,
had a similar one.

872
01:02:51,375 --> 01:02:53,125
That's all. Thank you.

873
01:02:54,083 --> 01:02:56,958
-What are you doing?
-Thank you, ma'am. You may leave.

874
01:02:58,041 --> 01:02:59,375
Thank you. Goodbye.

875
01:02:59,458 --> 01:03:03,458
Convert, Barreda. Only God can save you.

876
01:03:03,541 --> 01:03:05,166
Ma'am, leave the room.

877
01:03:05,250 --> 01:03:07,000
Ma'am, please.

878
01:03:08,208 --> 01:03:09,875
<i>Was he crazy? Was the abuse real?</i>

879
01:03:09,958 --> 01:03:11,916
<i>I won't make any statements.</i>

880
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:13,625
<i>Did those women abuse him?</i>

881
01:03:13,708 --> 01:03:16,458
<i>Everything's a lie, as I said.
That man's not crazy. Never was.</i>

882
01:03:16,541 --> 01:03:20,125
<i>Apparently, there's complete commotion
on this day of hearings.</i>

883
01:03:23,625 --> 01:03:25,291
How's the man of the hour doing?

884
01:03:25,375 --> 01:03:29,666
I can't believe what you're doing.
You're making me look like an idiot.

885
01:03:29,750 --> 01:03:30,916
Whose side are you on?

886
01:03:31,000 --> 01:03:33,916
You have two options.
You're either a nutjob or a piece of shit.

887
01:03:34,000 --> 01:03:37,500
We either prove you're incompetent
and they send you to a psychiatric clinic,

888
01:03:37,583 --> 01:03:40,833
or the fucking prosecutor
proves you planned everything

889
01:03:40,916 --> 01:03:42,166
so you could keep the house.

890
01:03:42,250 --> 01:03:43,958
And then you'll rot in prison.

891
01:03:49,375 --> 01:03:52,375
You're the boss here.

892
01:03:53,166 --> 01:03:54,916
But let me tell you something.

893
01:03:55,833 --> 01:03:58,958
Five years from now, I can guarantee
you'll be out on the streets,

894
01:03:59,041 --> 01:04:00,750
and that's all people will remember.

895
01:04:00,833 --> 01:04:01,833
Listen to me.

896
01:04:02,500 --> 01:04:05,083
You know what they were saying
on the radio on my way here?

897
01:04:05,166 --> 01:04:06,166
What?

898
01:04:06,875 --> 01:04:10,000
Barreda did what every Argentinian man
wishes he could do.

899
01:04:10,083 --> 01:04:12,041
He rebelled against his mother-in-law.

900
01:04:15,208 --> 01:04:17,666
Why do you think
so many people relate to you, Barreda?

901
01:04:18,708 --> 01:04:20,916
-Go, Barreda!
-Go, Pussy!

902
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:22,916
Are you the prisoners' dentist?

903
01:04:23,000 --> 01:04:26,000
Barreda, do abused men identify with you?

904
01:04:26,083 --> 01:04:28,958
<i>That's how Ricardo Barreda
appeared before court with his lawyer</i>

905
01:04:29,041 --> 01:04:33,541
<i>on a new day of hearings,
in a trial that divides public opinion.</i>

906
01:04:33,625 --> 01:04:35,750
<i>This is maybe the first time in history</i>

907
01:04:35,833 --> 01:04:39,541
<i>that someone who confessed to killing
his daughters gets so much public support.</i>

908
01:04:39,625 --> 01:04:41,333
Silence, please.

909
01:04:42,083 --> 01:04:43,083
Counselor.

910
01:04:46,250 --> 01:04:49,250
A delirious man lives in a reality
that he himself created.

911
01:04:49,333 --> 01:04:51,458
He will defend it by any means necessary.

912
01:04:51,541 --> 01:04:53,125
What's his justification?

913
01:04:53,791 --> 01:04:57,291
"They mistreated me,
they were mean," etcetera.

914
01:04:57,375 --> 01:05:00,375
Okay, Doctor, just to be clear.

915
01:05:00,458 --> 01:05:04,833
Are you saying Barreda wasn't
in his right mind when he did what he did?

916
01:05:04,916 --> 01:05:06,458
What I mean is

917
01:05:07,125 --> 01:05:12,250
Ricardo Barreda is suffering
from psychotic delusions of vindication.

918
01:05:12,333 --> 01:05:13,708
In other words, he's crazy.

919
01:05:14,291 --> 01:05:18,583
Exactly. He was crazy before the incident,
during the incident and now.

920
01:05:18,666 --> 01:05:20,666
Thank you. No more questions.

921
01:05:20,750 --> 01:05:22,750
-I'm not crazy.
-Silence, please.

922
01:05:24,541 --> 01:05:27,541
Yes. May I approach the bench?

923
01:05:27,625 --> 01:05:30,000
No, I should also be informed.

924
01:05:30,083 --> 01:05:32,541
-You can approach, too.
-Please.

925
01:05:34,166 --> 01:05:38,541
Given the expert's opinion,
and my client's condition,

926
01:05:38,625 --> 01:05:42,791
I ask the magistrates to let him
leave the room during the next testimony.

927
01:05:42,875 --> 01:05:46,500
-What do you think, Counselor?
-We could make an exception.

928
01:05:46,583 --> 01:05:49,458
-You think so?
-As an exception. I have no objection.

929
01:05:51,333 --> 01:05:53,833
-We will allow it as an exception.
-Thanks.

930
01:05:53,916 --> 01:05:55,291
I appreciate it.

931
01:05:56,041 --> 01:05:57,958
Débora, you may leave.

932
01:05:58,708 --> 01:06:02,083
-I'm not going anywhere.
-Listen to me. Trust me.

933
01:06:02,166 --> 01:06:03,291
We'll talk later.

934
01:06:05,208 --> 01:06:06,625
Let's go. I'll explain.

935
01:06:17,916 --> 01:06:20,375
-Barreda! A picture, please.
-Look over here, Barreda!

936
01:06:21,458 --> 01:06:23,708
Listen to me, girl.

937
01:06:23,791 --> 01:06:25,250
We shouldn't talk here.

938
01:06:28,416 --> 01:06:30,333
-There's Barreda.
-Barreda!

939
01:06:30,416 --> 01:06:33,041
-Here, Barreda!
-Where are they taking you?

940
01:06:33,625 --> 01:06:34,916
-Look over here.
-Barreda.

941
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:37,125
Barreda, why did you leave the courtroom?

942
01:06:37,208 --> 01:06:38,875
-Barreda.
-Look over here!

943
01:06:38,958 --> 01:06:40,666
Look here for a photo, Barreda!

944
01:06:40,750 --> 01:06:43,625
What would you say
to your supporters, Barreda?

945
01:06:45,916 --> 01:06:48,875
I'm with the patient in room number 23.

946
01:06:50,208 --> 01:06:51,333
-Barreda?
-Yes.

947
01:06:51,416 --> 01:06:54,458
-Okay.
-He's sleeping a lot, he barely moves.

948
01:06:54,541 --> 01:06:56,250
That's normal.

949
01:06:56,333 --> 01:06:59,958
He had a good night
and he's on the proper medication.

950
01:07:00,541 --> 01:07:04,250
He had an inguinal hernia surgery, right?

951
01:07:04,958 --> 01:07:07,500
I think with proper rest, he'll be fine.

952
01:07:07,583 --> 01:07:09,916
You have to avoid... Ma'am.

953
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:12,416
You must avoid
further injuries in that area...

954
01:07:13,291 --> 01:07:16,875
Do you want me to make notes for you
so you get them with the discharge papers?

955
01:07:16,958 --> 01:07:20,000
-Yes.
-Okay, we'll do that, then.

956
01:07:21,125 --> 01:07:23,750
I'll call his daughters
to let them know he's fine.

957
01:07:24,416 --> 01:07:26,166
There's a phone around the corner.

958
01:07:30,083 --> 01:07:32,541
They didn't even visit me.
Can you believe it?

959
01:07:32,625 --> 01:07:34,208
Of course, why would they come?

960
01:07:35,041 --> 01:07:36,791
They're conspiring against you.

961
01:07:37,416 --> 01:07:41,666
You were lucky this time, but...
Here, hide this. Don't let them find it.

962
01:07:44,083 --> 01:07:45,541
They'll destroy you.

963
01:07:47,291 --> 01:07:48,333
Holy Christ.

964
01:07:49,375 --> 01:07:50,833
You have to leave that place.

965
01:07:53,625 --> 01:07:56,208
I'm not going to get a divorce.

966
01:08:20,666 --> 01:08:23,916
I told you so. It was obvious.

967
01:08:26,500 --> 01:08:28,791
She's devastated.
How do you expect her to be?

968
01:08:28,875 --> 01:08:30,166
She saw that woman there.

969
01:08:33,208 --> 01:08:36,000
Sure. But I can't get into details now.

970
01:08:41,000 --> 01:08:42,750
Hang on a second.

971
01:08:43,458 --> 01:08:45,166
Rita agrees with me.

972
01:08:45,250 --> 01:08:47,000
He is slowly making you sick.

973
01:08:47,583 --> 01:08:49,166
You can't go on like this.

974
01:08:50,291 --> 01:08:51,291
Hello.

975
01:08:52,291 --> 01:08:55,958
Yes, I'll call you later
and we can talk some more, okay?

976
01:08:56,041 --> 01:08:58,750
We're not going to let this slide.

977
01:09:57,875 --> 01:09:59,916
Can you listen to me now?

978
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:01,625
How is this possible?

979
01:10:02,458 --> 01:10:05,291
The expert you brought in
is burying me up to my neck,

980
01:10:05,375 --> 01:10:07,333
and now you exclude me from my own trial.

981
01:10:07,416 --> 01:10:08,625
It's normal in these cases.

982
01:10:08,708 --> 01:10:10,333
-Sure, normal.
-Excuse me.

983
01:10:10,416 --> 01:10:11,250
It's all good.

984
01:10:11,333 --> 01:10:13,208
What's your boss doing now?

985
01:10:13,291 --> 01:10:15,166
What did he tell the judges?

986
01:10:15,250 --> 01:10:18,083
He's still insisting
on that "incompetent" bullshit.

987
01:10:18,166 --> 01:10:19,833
Can't you see he's driving me mad?

988
01:10:19,916 --> 01:10:22,875
-Who's the crazy one here?
-You're right.

989
01:10:22,958 --> 01:10:27,000
You're not crazy, you're a murderer,
and you should go to jail.

990
01:10:27,958 --> 01:10:30,000
Luckily, I'm not your lawyer,

991
01:10:30,083 --> 01:10:32,500
and my boss hasn't lost a case
in five years.

992
01:10:32,583 --> 01:10:34,708
If I were you, I'd follow his lead.

993
01:10:35,500 --> 01:10:36,708
Sit down, please.

994
01:10:38,958 --> 01:10:40,541
So you were playing dumb all along.

995
01:10:41,333 --> 01:10:44,791
You act all virtuous, but you're a bitch.

996
01:10:44,875 --> 01:10:47,958
-Got it.
-"Got it. Got it."

997
01:10:57,250 --> 01:11:00,166
We're on a break. We're doing great.

998
01:11:00,250 --> 01:11:02,541
Let's see if the prosecutor
can turn that one around.

999
01:11:02,625 --> 01:11:05,291
You told me people would believe me.

1000
01:11:05,375 --> 01:11:07,958
They do. Didn't you read the papers?
You're famous.

1001
01:11:08,041 --> 01:11:10,041
I can hear the bullshit you said in there.

1002
01:11:10,125 --> 01:11:12,916
Things are different in there.
What did I tell you?

1003
01:11:13,000 --> 01:11:15,958
If you want to get your freedom
and your house back,

1004
01:11:16,041 --> 01:11:18,625
claiming you're incompetent is key.

1005
01:11:18,708 --> 01:11:20,916
-Do we agree?
-Yes.

1006
01:11:21,000 --> 01:11:23,083
Okay, because there's something else.

1007
01:11:23,916 --> 01:11:27,041
Cáceres... don't.

1008
01:11:29,083 --> 01:11:31,583
Yes. The order in which
the deaths happened.

1009
01:11:31,666 --> 01:11:36,208
You need to say that the last person
you shot was one of your daughters.

1010
01:11:36,291 --> 01:11:39,875
-At the police station, I said...
-I don't give a fuck. Listen to me.

1011
01:11:41,083 --> 01:11:45,375
If the last person you shot was your wife
or your mother-in-law, you're fucked.

1012
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:47,958
You won't inherit anything.

1013
01:11:48,041 --> 01:11:49,250
Got it?

1014
01:11:49,333 --> 01:11:52,208
Okay. So, who did you shoot last?

1015
01:11:52,958 --> 01:11:54,458
-Cecilia.
-There.

1016
01:11:55,791 --> 01:11:57,333
Can you get us some coffee?

1017
01:12:15,291 --> 01:12:17,291
Well, the deed looks fine.

1018
01:12:18,583 --> 01:12:21,583
The property is under your name
and your husband's, right?

1019
01:12:22,291 --> 01:12:23,291
Yes.

1020
01:12:27,291 --> 01:12:30,375
We want to sell because one of the girls
is getting married,

1021
01:12:30,458 --> 01:12:31,875
and the other one's moving out.

1022
01:12:31,958 --> 01:12:35,166
It's a big house.
Too many square meters for us.

1023
01:12:35,250 --> 01:12:36,250
Sure.

1024
01:12:37,916 --> 01:12:38,916
Okay.

1025
01:12:40,666 --> 01:12:43,250
Can I take another look
around the ground floor?

1026
01:12:43,333 --> 01:12:44,250
Yes, of course.

1027
01:12:44,333 --> 01:12:45,166
-Yes?
-Yes.

1028
01:12:45,250 --> 01:12:46,250
Excuse me.

1029
01:12:48,750 --> 01:12:50,750
-May I go in?
-Yes, please.

1030
01:12:55,625 --> 01:12:57,583
If the buyer needs more space,

1031
01:12:57,666 --> 01:13:01,625
they can knock down this wall
and join the kitchen and the dining room.

1032
01:13:02,500 --> 01:13:04,666
They're doing that in Europe now.

1033
01:13:05,708 --> 01:13:07,416
It has potential.

1034
01:13:08,166 --> 01:13:10,041
Yes, it's really beautiful.

1035
01:13:10,125 --> 01:13:12,250
A great house for a family.

1036
01:13:15,625 --> 01:13:18,291
Okay, I'll call you in a few days
to give you an estimate.

1037
01:13:18,375 --> 01:13:20,708
And if we agree, we'll put it on sale.

1038
01:13:20,791 --> 01:13:22,791
-We'll publish the sale.
-Good afternoon.

1039
01:13:22,875 --> 01:13:23,916
Good afternoon.

1040
01:13:24,666 --> 01:13:27,791
-That's my husband.
-The gentleman is a real estate agent.

1041
01:13:27,875 --> 01:13:30,916
Sir, you have a beautiful property.

1042
01:13:31,000 --> 01:13:33,250
I promise we'll be able
to sell it quickly.

1043
01:13:34,875 --> 01:13:37,375
-Excuse me, I'll get my briefcase.
-Yes.

1044
01:13:43,833 --> 01:13:45,916
-Okay, thanks.
-You're welcome.

1045
01:13:46,000 --> 01:13:47,291
-Goodbye.
-I'll walk you out.

1046
01:13:47,375 --> 01:13:48,875
-Please.
-Bye.

1047
01:13:48,958 --> 01:13:50,083
Bye.

1048
01:13:56,000 --> 01:13:57,208
Great.

1049
01:13:58,000 --> 01:14:01,000
-Come, I need to tell you something.
-He liked it. He's gonna sell it.

1050
01:14:47,333 --> 01:14:48,416
Come in.

1051
01:14:52,375 --> 01:14:53,666
Excuse me.

1052
01:14:56,041 --> 01:14:58,250
Did they send you to talk to me?

1053
01:15:02,291 --> 01:15:04,541
No, I heard the music and came.

1054
01:15:05,875 --> 01:15:08,333
I was thinking the other day

1055
01:15:09,250 --> 01:15:11,958
about what kind of music
I want to play in my office.

1056
01:15:13,500 --> 01:15:19,083
Because playing ambient music
is a bit boring.

1057
01:15:19,833 --> 01:15:21,000
I don't know.

1058
01:15:22,041 --> 01:15:24,416
I play music to help my patients relax.

1059
01:15:26,000 --> 01:15:29,041
People think they're coming
to a torture chamber,

1060
01:15:29,833 --> 01:15:33,000
so I make them trust me.

1061
01:15:34,041 --> 01:15:35,125
Does it work?

1062
01:15:38,000 --> 01:15:39,416
Of course it works.

1063
01:15:40,208 --> 01:15:44,041
They're terrified when they come in,
but when they leave...

1064
01:15:48,166 --> 01:15:49,166
I'll take note of that.

1065
01:15:52,208 --> 01:15:53,583
Can I ask you a question?

1066
01:15:54,416 --> 01:15:55,583
Yes.

1067
01:15:55,666 --> 01:15:58,625
We have an extra room in the new house.

1068
01:15:59,958 --> 01:16:03,250
And I'm setting up my office there.

1069
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:06,833
Something small just to start.

1070
01:16:09,166 --> 01:16:12,458
Remember you offered me your chair?

1071
01:16:13,833 --> 01:16:15,416
The old one, not this one.

1072
01:16:17,125 --> 01:16:20,916
It would really help me
because it's the most expensive thing.

1073
01:16:25,416 --> 01:16:26,541
Can I take it?

1074
01:16:27,625 --> 01:16:31,625
But for more invasive treatments,

1075
01:16:32,541 --> 01:16:35,583
a root canal, a removal,

1076
01:16:36,916 --> 01:16:38,083
never play opera.

1077
01:16:38,750 --> 01:16:42,250
Too dramatic. They'll never loosen up.

1078
01:16:43,166 --> 01:16:44,166
Sure.

1079
01:16:45,875 --> 01:16:47,333
Are you sure about this?

1080
01:16:50,208 --> 01:16:52,791
Are you really moving in
with that young man?

1081
01:16:53,708 --> 01:16:56,250
I mean, if you're sure,

1082
01:16:57,750 --> 01:16:59,375
go ahead, but...

1083
01:17:02,708 --> 01:17:03,875
Yes, I'm sure.

1084
01:17:23,791 --> 01:17:24,791
Okay.

1085
01:17:25,666 --> 01:17:26,708
I've had enough.

1086
01:17:29,416 --> 01:17:30,416
What?

1087
01:17:30,458 --> 01:17:32,291
You decide to ruin your life

1088
01:17:32,375 --> 01:17:36,208
by moving in with an older man
who has a daughter,

1089
01:17:36,291 --> 01:17:39,625
and you come here
asking for my chair to start working?

1090
01:17:39,708 --> 01:17:41,500
Why don't you ask him?

1091
01:17:42,416 --> 01:17:44,958
Why didn't you save up some money
like we all did?

1092
01:17:47,041 --> 01:17:49,750
Unless they already told you
they want to sell this house

1093
01:17:49,833 --> 01:17:52,333
and you thought you'd get money from that.

1094
01:17:52,416 --> 01:17:54,291
Did those two tell you that?

1095
01:17:57,291 --> 01:17:58,625
They didn't say anything.

1096
01:18:04,791 --> 01:18:07,291
Sunday is my last lunch here at home.

1097
01:18:08,166 --> 01:18:09,416
Gastón is coming.

1098
01:18:10,375 --> 01:18:11,791
You can be there, or not.

1099
01:18:46,000 --> 01:18:48,041
You're not taking these.

1100
01:18:48,125 --> 01:18:49,333
What's wrong?

1101
01:18:55,000 --> 01:18:56,833
He ruins every happy moment.

1102
01:18:56,916 --> 01:18:58,125
What did he say?

1103
01:19:02,291 --> 01:19:03,875
Tell me, what did he say?

1104
01:19:07,583 --> 01:19:11,541
Remember he offered me the old chair?

1105
01:19:11,625 --> 01:19:12,625
Yes.

1106
01:19:14,583 --> 01:19:16,583
Well, he won't give it to me now.

1107
01:19:16,666 --> 01:19:19,500
He says I'll ruin my life
with Gastón, and...

1108
01:19:20,458 --> 01:19:24,041
that he has a daughter, that the house...
That I should've saved up.

1109
01:19:24,125 --> 01:19:25,833
Ceci, don't pay attention to him.

1110
01:19:26,708 --> 01:19:27,750
I'm sick of it.

1111
01:19:28,958 --> 01:19:31,708
Listen to me. You're leaving.

1112
01:19:31,791 --> 01:19:36,291
You're going to start a new life,
and your own family, Ceci.

1113
01:19:36,375 --> 01:19:37,416
-That's beautiful.
-Yes.

1114
01:19:38,416 --> 01:19:41,416
-I don't want you to see me like this.
-No.

1115
01:19:41,500 --> 01:19:44,166
-I've seen you so many times like this.
-Yes, I know.

1116
01:19:47,375 --> 01:19:49,875
-I love you.
-Me too. I'll miss you.

1117
01:19:49,958 --> 01:19:51,291
Me too. So much.

1118
01:19:59,041 --> 01:20:00,625
He left.

1119
01:20:03,708 --> 01:20:05,833
Asshole. Fuck him.

1120
01:20:06,541 --> 01:20:07,750
Idiot.

1121
01:20:32,291 --> 01:20:34,291
-Let's go.
-Come with me, Barreda.

1122
01:20:44,791 --> 01:20:45,958
Go, Barreda!

1123
01:20:47,083 --> 01:20:48,250
Keep quiet!

1124
01:20:48,333 --> 01:20:51,166
- Go, Barreda,
- Silence!

1125
01:20:51,250 --> 01:20:52,416
Quiet down!

1126
01:20:56,750 --> 01:20:58,916
May I have some water, please?

1127
01:21:00,458 --> 01:21:01,541
Excuse me.

1128
01:21:14,791 --> 01:21:15,875
Thanks.

1129
01:21:15,958 --> 01:21:18,375
The prosecutor will now take over.
Go ahead.

1130
01:21:19,375 --> 01:21:24,875
Barreda, do you think these deaths
could have been avoided?

1131
01:21:25,875 --> 01:21:28,000
We all could've tried
to avoid what happened.

1132
01:21:28,083 --> 01:21:30,500
I'm talking about you.
Could you have avoided them?

1133
01:21:30,583 --> 01:21:32,500
-No, not me.
-Why?

1134
01:21:33,208 --> 01:21:38,125
Because of the humiliation,

1135
01:21:38,875 --> 01:21:41,333
the moral degradation,

1136
01:21:41,416 --> 01:21:45,041
the shame, and all those things...

1137
01:21:45,875 --> 01:21:47,291
No, I don't know.

1138
01:21:49,125 --> 01:21:51,833
I was already convinced.
It was either them or me.

1139
01:21:53,458 --> 01:21:54,833
Would you do it again?

1140
01:21:56,458 --> 01:22:00,125
Barreda, would you murder them again
if you could right now?

1141
01:22:03,791 --> 01:22:05,708
-Right now?
-Yes.

1142
01:22:06,625 --> 01:22:09,333
No, because that's...

1143
01:22:10,458 --> 01:22:12,625
-No.
-Because they're already dead.

1144
01:22:12,708 --> 01:22:16,041
No... No, that's...

1145
01:22:17,291 --> 01:22:19,583
Are you being serious, or are you joking?

1146
01:22:20,750 --> 01:22:22,916
How am I supposed to answer that?

1147
01:22:23,000 --> 01:22:25,125
However you want.
You have the right to answer.

1148
01:22:25,208 --> 01:22:27,333
-Please, mind your manners.
-However I want?

1149
01:22:27,416 --> 01:22:31,958
-Go on, answer. I think you understood.
-Yes, I understood perfectly.

1150
01:22:33,666 --> 01:22:36,125
-You said you're not sorry.
-Suggestive question.

1151
01:22:36,208 --> 01:22:41,166
Because that was a unique
and unrepeatable situation!

1152
01:22:41,250 --> 01:22:42,875
-Is that clear?
-So you'd do it again.

1153
01:22:42,958 --> 01:22:44,666
Let's have some order.

1154
01:22:44,750 --> 01:22:49,458
I was able to have a harmonious dialogue
with the judges, but not with you.

1155
01:22:51,416 --> 01:22:52,833
No more questions.

1156
01:23:01,208 --> 01:23:02,333
After you.

1157
01:23:05,875 --> 01:23:07,333
-Good evening.
-Good evening.

1158
01:23:07,416 --> 01:23:09,125
Through that door over there.

1159
01:23:09,208 --> 01:23:10,583
It's starting.

1160
01:23:12,916 --> 01:23:14,125
Thanks.

1161
01:23:32,750 --> 01:23:34,083
This is unbelievable.

1162
01:23:34,166 --> 01:23:37,541
-Isn't that Barreda?
-No, it can't be.

1163
01:23:37,625 --> 01:23:38,625
Excuse me.

1164
01:23:39,708 --> 01:23:40,583
Sorry.

1165
01:23:40,666 --> 01:23:41,791
Yes, it's him.

1166
01:23:42,958 --> 01:23:43,958
Sorry.

1167
01:23:51,208 --> 01:23:52,750
No, Mom.

1168
01:23:52,833 --> 01:23:54,041
Stay here.

1169
01:23:54,125 --> 01:23:55,125
Son of a bitch.

1170
01:23:55,208 --> 01:23:56,333
Don't move.

1171
01:24:05,250 --> 01:24:07,416
Here. Take it.

1172
01:24:34,791 --> 01:24:35,875
Ricardo.

1173
01:24:39,250 --> 01:24:40,250
It's over.

1174
01:24:41,416 --> 01:24:44,750
After Cecilia and Adriana move out,
we're getting a divorce.

1175
01:24:45,333 --> 01:24:49,333
I can't take it anymore.
Why did you have to bring that woman?

1176
01:24:51,875 --> 01:24:53,250
I believed you.

1177
01:24:53,333 --> 01:24:56,541
I convinced myself time and time again
that things would get better.

1178
01:24:56,625 --> 01:24:59,125
But it's useless. You don't care.

1179
01:24:59,958 --> 01:25:01,958
You crossed the line today.

1180
01:25:03,208 --> 01:25:04,958
I'm going to see a lawyer.

1181
01:25:29,541 --> 01:25:31,833
{\an8}BARREDA IS INNOCENT

1182
01:25:49,708 --> 01:25:52,958
<i>Today, Barreda will declare in front
of the judges for the last time.</i>

1183
01:25:53,041 --> 01:25:54,500
<i>The anticipation is huge</i>

1184
01:25:54,583 --> 01:25:58,125
<i>to hear him recount
all the details of the day of the crime.</i>

1185
01:25:58,208 --> 01:26:00,625
<i>By explaining
what really happened that day,</i>

1186
01:26:00,708 --> 01:26:02,958
<i>Barreda will be closer to his freedom.</i>

1187
01:26:03,041 --> 01:26:06,583
<i>Now we just need to wait
for the judges' decision.</i>

1188
01:26:09,083 --> 01:26:12,875
Barreda, do you remember
how that Sunday started?

1189
01:26:26,666 --> 01:26:30,416
<i>You have reached Dr. Barreda's office.</i>

1190
01:26:30,500 --> 01:26:34,583
No, it'll always be sour
if you use that one.

1191
01:26:34,666 --> 01:26:37,791
<i>-opening hours, Monday to Friday...</i>
-Mom.

1192
01:26:37,875 --> 01:26:39,541
Add some sugar.

1193
01:26:39,625 --> 01:26:42,958
<i>Or leave a message after the beep. Thanks.</i>

1194
01:26:43,666 --> 01:26:45,750
<i>-Hello.</i>
-Good morning, honey.

1195
01:26:45,833 --> 01:26:47,125
Good morning, Grandma.

1196
01:26:47,208 --> 01:26:48,458
<i>It's me, Martín.</i>

1197
01:26:48,541 --> 01:26:51,166
<i>I wanted to know if I should pick you up.</i>

1198
01:26:51,250 --> 01:26:54,125
-Hi, baby, how are you?
<i>-Hi, honey, all good?</i>

1199
01:26:54,208 --> 01:26:55,208
All good.

1200
01:26:55,291 --> 01:26:58,416
<i>I'm glad. Will you have lunch there
or what will you do?</i>

1201
01:26:58,500 --> 01:26:59,666
<i>I'm having lunch here.</i>

1202
01:26:59,750 --> 01:27:02,041
<i>But we'll go to the movies
afterwards, right?</i>

1203
01:27:02,125 --> 01:27:05,750
<i>Yes, maybe. But later.
It's so sunny today.</i>

1204
01:27:07,833 --> 01:27:11,833
Barreda, was there a reason
you picked that Sunday?

1205
01:27:13,375 --> 01:27:14,375
No.

1206
01:27:15,166 --> 01:27:17,208
I didn't know when I was going to do it.

1207
01:27:18,708 --> 01:27:22,041
Since I had my hernia surgery,

1208
01:27:23,250 --> 01:27:28,333
I'd been having this horrible thought
that was getting bigger every day.

1209
01:27:29,750 --> 01:27:32,250
It was inevitable.

1210
01:27:45,625 --> 01:27:49,250
Last breakfast
for the spoiled one in the house.

1211
01:27:49,916 --> 01:27:54,208
You brought me breakfast, Baba! So nice!

1212
01:27:54,291 --> 01:27:56,833
-What are you looking at?
-Look what I found.

1213
01:27:57,541 --> 01:27:58,833
We were so little.

1214
01:27:58,916 --> 01:28:00,666
-So little.
-Right?

1215
01:28:01,458 --> 01:28:03,833
Do you remember what the trigger was?

1216
01:28:07,375 --> 01:28:10,166
When did you think
that was the right moment?

1217
01:28:43,083 --> 01:28:44,375
I was listening to that.

1218
01:28:45,375 --> 01:28:47,208
We were all listening to that.

1219
01:28:47,291 --> 01:28:48,750
My head's exploding.

1220
01:28:51,000 --> 01:28:52,166
Ricardo.

1221
01:28:52,958 --> 01:28:56,583
Why don't you go prune the vine?
You have time today.

1222
01:28:56,666 --> 01:28:58,208
"Narrow or reduced."

1223
01:28:58,291 --> 01:28:59,666
Is this guy coming for lunch?

1224
01:28:59,750 --> 01:29:02,875
-Narrow, reduced...
-"Slim"? I'll put this over here.

1225
01:29:02,958 --> 01:29:04,375
Okay.

1226
01:29:05,458 --> 01:29:06,833
No, it doesn't fit.

1227
01:29:06,916 --> 01:29:09,083
Yes, he's coming. His name is Gastón.

1228
01:29:09,791 --> 01:29:13,333
-I don't like that guy.
-Don't start, it's Sunday.

1229
01:29:13,875 --> 01:29:16,041
"Tight." Of course, I'm so dumb.

1230
01:29:16,125 --> 01:29:17,208
And Cecilia?

1231
01:29:18,708 --> 01:29:20,625
Packing up since 6:00 a.m.

1232
01:29:22,583 --> 01:29:24,833
She can continue later.
Tell her to come down.

1233
01:29:24,916 --> 01:29:27,125
-What for?
-For breakfast.

1234
01:29:28,041 --> 01:29:29,333
She already had breakfast.

1235
01:29:30,083 --> 01:29:32,250
Why don't you occupy yourself
with something?

1236
01:29:35,333 --> 01:29:36,416
Cecilia!

1237
01:29:37,208 --> 01:29:38,750
-Cecilia!
-Ricardo.

1238
01:29:38,833 --> 01:29:39,958
What are you doing?

1239
01:29:40,583 --> 01:29:42,000
I'll kill you if you bother her.

1240
01:29:43,125 --> 01:29:45,083
Go take care of the vine.

1241
01:29:45,166 --> 01:29:48,416
I'll clean the front porch.
It's so dirty that it's embarrassing.

1242
01:29:48,500 --> 01:29:49,833
Do whatever you want.

1243
01:29:49,916 --> 01:29:54,958
If you want to clean all day like a maid,
go ahead. Just don't bother her.

1244
01:29:58,916 --> 01:30:01,125
<i>My wife told me...</i>

1245
01:30:01,916 --> 01:30:04,333
that if I bothered my daughter,
she'd kill me.

1246
01:30:06,625 --> 01:30:08,583
And what did you say?

1247
01:30:10,750 --> 01:30:11,958
Nothing.

1248
01:30:12,541 --> 01:30:15,875
I just want to have breakfast in peace.

1249
01:30:15,958 --> 01:30:17,083
Fine.

1250
01:30:17,166 --> 01:30:19,458
It doesn't matter. What do you want?
I don't get it.

1251
01:30:20,041 --> 01:30:25,625
The vine is overgrown.
We have to go up there and fix the guide.

1252
01:30:25,708 --> 01:30:28,166
But I can't, my arms get tired.

1253
01:30:28,833 --> 01:30:32,625
You don't give a damn
if I fall and smash my head.

1254
01:30:32,708 --> 01:30:35,333
Hi? Honey, did something happen?

1255
01:30:38,375 --> 01:30:40,708
Oh, no. Poor thing.

1256
01:30:42,541 --> 01:30:43,750
What's her temperature?

1257
01:30:45,583 --> 01:30:46,875
Oh, I'm sorry.

1258
01:30:47,541 --> 01:30:50,000
No, it's fine. We'll do it another day.

1259
01:30:50,833 --> 01:30:52,708
What time are the movers coming tomorrow?

1260
01:30:53,666 --> 01:30:54,750
Perfect.

1261
01:30:55,958 --> 01:30:57,708
Sure. I'll tell Mom.

1262
01:30:57,791 --> 01:30:59,208
Me too. Bye.

1263
01:31:00,083 --> 01:31:02,250
What happened? Who were you talking to?

1264
01:31:02,333 --> 01:31:05,541
It was Gastón. He won't be able to come.
His daughter has a fever.

1265
01:31:06,458 --> 01:31:09,375
Better. I mean,
I'm sorry for the girl, but...

1266
01:31:09,458 --> 01:31:11,875
-Some other time will be better.
-Yes.

1267
01:31:11,958 --> 01:31:14,666
-Go. Finish packing.
-Okay.

1268
01:31:17,375 --> 01:31:20,541
You too, go do whatever you have to do.
Don't look at me like that.

1269
01:31:34,583 --> 01:31:36,708
<i>Then, she said to me,</i>

1270
01:31:36,791 --> 01:31:42,666
<i>"Go clean the house.
That's all you're good at, Pussy."</i>

1271
01:31:45,250 --> 01:31:46,666
What happened then?

1272
01:31:47,291 --> 01:31:53,083
I said, "Pussy will go fix the vine,
since that's what you all want."

1273
01:31:54,708 --> 01:32:01,250
So, I went to get the hand pruners,

1274
01:32:01,333 --> 01:32:07,000
<i>and I found the shotgun in the basement.</i>

1275
01:32:09,708 --> 01:32:13,416
<i>And I felt like...</i>

1276
01:32:14,291 --> 01:32:17,583
Like a force compelling me to pick it up.

1277
01:32:18,375 --> 01:32:23,625
So I picked it up,
went to the kitchen and shot.

1278
01:32:25,791 --> 01:32:26,791
And then?

1279
01:32:30,541 --> 01:32:37,458
My mother-in-law was coming down
from the second floor...

1280
01:32:38,750 --> 01:32:40,333
and...

1281
01:32:41,833 --> 01:32:43,250
I shot her.

1282
01:32:45,041 --> 01:32:51,375
In your first statement to the police,
you said you shot your daughter first,

1283
01:32:51,458 --> 01:32:53,458
and your mother-in-law last.

1284
01:32:55,750 --> 01:32:58,708
I don't know. I'm not sure.

1285
01:33:02,958 --> 01:33:07,666
"Mythological figure who used
a thread to get out of a labyrinth."

1286
01:33:12,291 --> 01:33:13,291
Mom!

1287
01:33:40,125 --> 01:33:41,166
Ceci.

1288
01:33:41,875 --> 01:33:42,875
Ceci.

1289
01:33:43,958 --> 01:33:45,333
-Did you hear that?
-What?

1290
01:33:45,416 --> 01:33:47,583
-Did you hear that?
-Stay here.

1291
01:35:33,666 --> 01:35:35,708
<i>How can a family man,</i>

1292
01:35:36,875 --> 01:35:40,166
<i>a prestigious dentist,</i>

1293
01:35:40,250 --> 01:35:43,375
<i>be capable of carrying out
such a bloodbath?</i>

1294
01:35:44,541 --> 01:35:48,833
That's what the whole country
was wondering during this trial.

1295
01:35:48,916 --> 01:35:53,000
Ricardo Barreda suffers
from a serious delusional disorder.

1296
01:35:53,083 --> 01:35:54,083
He is delirious.

1297
01:35:54,541 --> 01:35:58,333
He's absolutely convinced
that what happened had to happen,

1298
01:35:59,291 --> 01:36:02,916
as if a higher deterministic force
guided his actions.

1299
01:36:03,541 --> 01:36:05,875
Delirium? Abuse?

1300
01:36:06,625 --> 01:36:10,416
None of that could be proved,
because none of it was real.

1301
01:36:11,125 --> 01:36:14,625
This quadruple murder
was a calculated violent incident.

1302
01:36:15,208 --> 01:36:18,875
<i>He chose that day because it was the last
day the four of them were together.</i>

1303
01:36:19,666 --> 01:36:20,958
<i>He fabricated an alibi.</i>

1304
01:36:21,041 --> 01:36:22,958
<i>First, I went to the zoo.</i>

1305
01:36:23,041 --> 01:36:26,083
The giraffe is my favorite animal.

1306
01:36:26,750 --> 01:36:29,541
<i>He kept the admission ticket as evidence.</i>

1307
01:36:30,166 --> 01:36:34,166
<i>He planned dates to have witnesses
to every step he took that day.</i>

1308
01:36:34,916 --> 01:36:38,333
<i>He made a reservation in one of the most
popular pizza restaurants in La Plata.</i>

1309
01:36:39,208 --> 01:36:43,708
<i>He meticulously chose the people
who would help him get rid of the evidence</i>

1310
01:36:43,791 --> 01:36:46,250
<i>and the most remote place to do it
without being seen.</i>

1311
01:36:48,333 --> 01:36:50,458
<i>Everything was premeditated.</i>

1312
01:36:52,458 --> 01:36:55,291
<i>Some robbers broke into my house.
There are four bodies.</i>

1313
01:36:57,541 --> 01:36:59,458
<i>Having an alibi, even to convince oneself,</i>

1314
01:36:59,541 --> 01:37:02,333
is typical in a transient delirium.

1315
01:37:03,000 --> 01:37:05,625
<i>Sure, that's why he confessed
that same day.</i>

1316
01:37:05,708 --> 01:37:08,791
Look, you can be crazy
and fabricate an alibi.

1317
01:37:08,875 --> 01:37:10,666
-Is that correct?
-Yes, that's correct.

1318
01:37:11,250 --> 01:37:13,250
This crime was marked by cruelty,

1319
01:37:13,958 --> 01:37:15,125
by premeditation,

1320
01:37:16,166 --> 01:37:17,166
and by greed.

1321
01:37:18,041 --> 01:37:22,291
From the very beginning,
Barreda showed a composed coldness.

1322
01:37:23,625 --> 01:37:30,166
His actions are typical of someone
who deeply hates the women in his family.

1323
01:37:30,250 --> 01:37:33,166
It would be more reassuring
if only crazy people were murderers,

1324
01:37:33,250 --> 01:37:34,750
but it's not like that.

1325
01:37:34,833 --> 01:37:37,375
Barreda has his own ethics, his own rules.

1326
01:37:37,458 --> 01:37:41,416
And by these rules, he killed four women.

1327
01:37:43,208 --> 01:37:46,875
Society already understood
that Barreda was driven crazy.

1328
01:37:46,958 --> 01:37:49,166
He needs to be treated.

1329
01:37:49,250 --> 01:37:53,750
I ask the judges to sentence
Mr. Ricardo Barreda to life sentence.

1330
01:37:53,833 --> 01:37:56,625
I ask the judges
to declare him incompetent.

1331
01:37:56,708 --> 01:38:01,875
<i>That's what the people are asking.
Justice for this man.</i>

1332
01:38:04,208 --> 01:38:06,250
<i>Barreda murdered his entire family.</i>

1333
01:38:07,916 --> 01:38:12,291
If he is not convicted,
what message are we sending to society?

1334
01:38:55,458 --> 01:39:01,333
<i>This afternoon, the court sentenced
Ricardo Barreda to life imprisonment.</i>

1335
01:39:01,416 --> 01:39:04,375
The ruling, that had...

1336
01:39:04,458 --> 01:39:06,791
How do you feel
about the sentence, Barreda?

1337
01:39:06,875 --> 01:39:09,625
Voting in favor of criminal liability.
He's coming out.

1338
01:39:11,208 --> 01:39:13,000
You're my idol!

1339
01:39:13,708 --> 01:39:15,333
Did the sentence surprise you?

1340
01:39:15,416 --> 01:39:16,875
-Barreda!
-Son of a bitch!

1341
01:39:16,958 --> 01:39:18,416
Here, take it!

1342
01:39:19,083 --> 01:39:21,708
You'll die in prison.
What do you think about that?

1343
01:39:24,250 --> 01:39:25,875
Murderer!

1344
01:39:29,458 --> 01:39:31,500
-Murderer!
-You're great!

1345
01:39:31,583 --> 01:39:33,750
You're amazing, Barreda!

1346
01:39:33,833 --> 01:39:35,000
Piece of shit!

1347
01:39:38,500 --> 01:39:40,416
You're my idol, Pussy!

1348
01:39:43,500 --> 01:39:47,333
After spending only 17 years in prison,
Ricardo Barreda got his freedom back.

1349
01:39:47,416 --> 01:39:50,625
He remarried and died at age 84.

1350
01:39:50,708 --> 01:39:57,083
Even today, he's admired
with a mix of devotion and irony.

1351
01:39:59,583 --> 01:40:03,416
At the time of their deaths, Elena Arreche
was 86, Gladys McDonald, 56,

1352
01:40:03,500 --> 01:40:05,916
Cecilia Barreda, 26,
and Adriana Barreda, 24.

1353
01:40:06,000 --> 01:40:09,416
Very little was known about them,
and their portrayal in this film

1354
01:40:09,500 --> 01:40:14,333
is based on public statements
of those who knew them.

1355
01:45:19,000 --> 01:45:21,000
Subtitle translation by MC Irazoqui
